prompt:
Implement a 3D fish sorting game using Three.js. Drag the fish into the correct containers according to size.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/BarramundiFish.glb;
(2) Clone 10 fish in 3 sizes: small (scale 0.5, 4 fish), medium (scale 1.0, 3 fish), and large (scale 1.5, 3 fish);
(3) Scatter them randomly across the upper area of the scene;

[Sorting Containers]
(4) Use 3 translucent boxes (BoxGeometry) as containers, labeled "Small"/"Medium"/"Large";
(5) Arrange the containers in a row in the lower area of the scene;

[Drag Interaction]
(6) Use Raycaster to detect clicks on fish;
(7) Hold down the mouse button and drag a fish to move it on a horizontal plane;
(8) When the mouse button is released, detect whether the fish is above a container;
(9) Correct sorting: the fish turns green, 10 points are added, and it drops into the container;
(10) Incorrect sorting: the fish turns red, 5 points are deducted, and it snaps back to its original position;

[Timer]
(11) A 90-second countdown (id="timer");
(12) When time runs out, the game ends and displays the final score;

[HUD Display]
(13) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Score (id="score")
  - Sorted count (id="sorted")
  - Accuracy (id="accuracy")
  - Remaining time (id="timer")

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean
  - score: number
  - sortedCount: number
  - accuracy: number (0-100%)
  - timeRemaining: number (seconds)
  - fishRemaining: number

Output a single standalone HTML file.
